<misterromdescription>
    <name>Neck-N-Neck (v1.2)</name>
    <setname>neckneck</setname>
    <rbf>Gm0rk_ITech8</rbf>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <mratimestamp>20261004</mratimestamp>
    <year>1992</year>
    <manufacturer>Bundra Games / Incredible Technologies</manufacturer>
    <category>Sports / Horse Racing</category>
    <players>1</players>
    <joystick>none</joystick>
    <rotation>horizontal</rotation>
    <num_buttons>7</num_buttons>
    <buttons names="Horse 1,Horse 2,Horse 3,Horse 4,Horse 5,Horse 6,Start,Coin,Service" default="A,B,X,Y,L,R,Start,Select"/>

    <romstruct>
Board select (ioctl index 1): 0B = itech8 6809 board (3), 64 KB program
(bit 3), horizontal; second byte 0B = MAME's lo memory map (bit 0), 2
page large display at 8 MHz (bits 2-1 = 1), YM3812 sound board with a
PIA (bits 4-3 = 1); third byte 08 = Neck-N-Neck's inputs.
Download stream (ioctl index 0), 1,146,880 bytes:
000000 - 007FFF   32K  sound program                  -> block RAM
008000 - 017FFF   64K  main program                   -> SDRAM bank 0
018000 - 057FFF  256K  OKI samples                    -> SDRAM bank 2
058000 - 117FFF  768K  graphics ROM region (512K used)-> SDRAM bank 1
    </romstruct>

    <rom index="1">
        <part>0B 0B 08</part>
    </rom>

    <rom index="0" zip="neckneck.zip" md5="7356857592fad295209baabbdb3fea1e">
        <!-- sound program (sound CPU $8000-$FFFF) -->
        <part name="nn_snd10.u27" crc="74771b2f"/>
        <!-- main program (64 KB: banks at $4000, last 32 KB at $8000) -->
        <part name="nn_prg12.u5" crc="8e51734a"/>
        <!-- OKI M6295 samples -->
        <part name="nn_srom0.bin" crc="33687201"/>
        <!-- graphics ROMs -->
        <part name="nn_grom0.bin" crc="064d1464"/>
        <part name="nn_grom1.bin" crc="622d9a0b"/>
        <part name="nn_grom2.bin" crc="e7eb4020"/>
        <part name="nn_grom3.bin" crc="765c8593"/>
        <part repeat="0x40000">00</part>
    </rom>

    <!-- 8 KB battery-backed RAM (CPU $2000-$3FFF) -->
    <nvram index="4" size="8192"/>
</misterromdescription>
